A couple weeks ago, I had an idea for a patch to add a command called,
well, "#command" or something similar, which would allow you to enter
a word to "command" your pets.  What I was thinking was something
along these lines:

"attack" - On the next turn, pet has a chance of attacking even a
monster it would normally ignore.

"heel" - For 1d5 turns, pet has a chance of _not_ attacking peaceful
monsters.

It seems like it might be a bit more difficult to code than what
you're suggesting, but I think this would be a lot more balanced than
a patch that simply causes pets to never attack peacefuls, which would
be annoying more often than it would be helpful, I think.

Perhaps intelligent pets of L alignment should _never_ attack
peacefuls?  That would make for interesting game balance.  Then again,
most of the good pets are C anyhow...

